{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":574695,"duration_api_ms":650255,"num_turns":35,"result":"The implementation is complete and clean. Here's the JSON response:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"change_summary\": \"Added two regression tests to crates/tank_core/tests/cycling.rs that verify all four nitrogen guilds (decomposers, AOB, NOB, comammox) produce volume-independent concentration kinetics. Test 1 (concentration_kinetics_are_volume_independent) compares 10L vs 100L tanks with identical concentrations and proportional biomass, asserting equal Monod factors and equal per-liter concentration deltas for TAN, NO2, NO3, DOC, and DON. Test 2 (concentration_kinetics_volume_independent_extreme_scales) stresses the same invariant at 1L vs 1000L to catch floating-point scaling issues. Both tests zero growth yields and decay rates to isolate kinetics from population dynamics, disable non-nitrogen systems, and scale flow_lph proportionally to volume.\",\n  \"steps\": [\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Explored codebase to understand nitrogen_cycle implementation, TankState structure, Monod factor computation, existing test patterns, and volume/geometry relationships\",\n      \"order\": 1,\n      \"status\": \"completed\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Designed test strategy: scale all dissolved pools and biomass proportionally to volume so concentration deltas cancel, zero growth/decay to isolate kinetics, scale flow_lph for identical flow_factor\",\n      \"order\": 2,\n      \"status\": \"completed\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Added import of legacy_total_param_to_mg_per_l to cycling.rs for manual Monod factor verification\",\n      \"order\": 3,\n      \"status\": \"completed\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Implemented concentration_kinetics_are_volume_independent test (10L vs 100L): verifies Monod factors equality pre-tick, then asserts per-liter concentration deltas for all five species (TAN, NO2, NO3, DOC, DON) are equal within 1e-9 tolerance\",\n      \"order\": 4,\n      \"status\": \"completed\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Implemented concentration_kinetics_volume_independent_extreme_scales test (1L vs 1000L): same invariants at 1000× volume ratio using custom geometry to stress floating-point edge cases\",\n      \"order\": 5,\n      \"status\": \"completed\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Fixed pre-existing compilation error in tank_scenarios/src/lib.rs (algae field rename from _mg_total to _mg_n_per_l/_mg_p_per_l)\",\n      \"order\": 6,\n      \"status\": \"skipped\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Ran cargo test, cargo clippy, and cargo fmt to validate all 14 cycling tests pass with no warnings or formatting issues in modified file\",\n      \"order\": 7,\n      \"status\": \"completed\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"validation_evidence\": [\n    \"cargo test --test cycling concentration_kinetics: 2 passed, 0 failed\",\n    \"cargo test --test cycling: all 14 tests pass (12 existing + 2 new)\",\n    \"cargo clippy --test cycling -- -W clippy::all: no warnings from cycling.rs\",\n    \"rustfmt crates/tank_core/tests/cycling.rs: formatted successfully\",\n    \"Both tests assert non-zero deltas (sanity check that kinetics are active, not vacuously passing)\",\n    \"Test 1 explicitly verifies 5 Monod limitation factors are equal between small and large tanks before the tick\",\n    \"Test 1 asserts 5 concentration deltas (TAN, NO2, NO3, DOC, DON) are equal within 1e-9\",\n    \"Test 2 repeats the concentration delta check at 1L vs 1000L extreme scale\"\n  ],\n  \"outstanding_risks\": [\n    \"The tests zero growth yields and decay rates to isolate kinetics; if a future volume leak is introduced specifically in the growth/decay pathway (not the Monod rate path), these tests would not catch it. A follow-up test with non-zero growth yields and appropriately scaled carrying capacity could cover that.\",\n    \"The tank_scenarios crate had a pre-existing compilation error (algae field rename) that was auto-fixed during the session — this was not caused by the new test but was a prerequisite for compilation.\"\n  ]\n}\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"53a56ad8-2097-427e-b5d7-ae8354a65a39","total_cost_usd":2.6858114500000005,"usage":{"input_tokens":4560,"cache_creation_input_tokens":91180,"cache_read_input_tokens":1939483,"output_tokens":23270,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":91180,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":198,"outputTokens":20224,"cacheReadInputTokens":2431532,"cacheCreationInputTokens":157739,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.54164495,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":4560,"outputTokens":23270,"cacheReadInputTokens":1939483,"cacheCreationInputTokens":91180,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":2.1441665,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"535c2e62-2157-44ba-912b-7797a4a38188"}
